{"schema":4,"id":"0625_2026FM_12_q24","paper":{"syllabus":"0625","session":"2026-FM","code":"0625/12","paper":1,"variant":2},"number":24,"type":"mcq","marks":1,"answer":"D","same_as":[],"parts":[{"path":"24","label":null,"parent":null,"marks":1,"text":"Satellite phones can use two types of satellite: ● geostationary satellites at a height of about 36 000 km ● or fast-moving low orbit satellites at a height of about 1000 km. Why do geostationary satellite phones have noticeable delays in conversations during phone calls, but low orbit satellite phones do not ? A Microwaves are carried along faster by low orbit satellites. B Microwaves are only transmitted by the phone when a geostationary satellite is overhead. C Microwaves used by low orbit satellites are faster than microwaves used by geostationary satellites. D Microwaves travelling at the same high speed take longer to travel to and from geostationary satellites than to and from low orbit satellites.","layout":[{"src":{"doc":"qp","page":9,"box":[30.0,185.0,570.0,403.5]},"w":540.0,"h":218.5,"text":[{"t":"24","x":19.56,"y":13.96,"w":12.25,"s":11.04,"f":"sans","b":1,"role":"qnum"},{"t":"Satellite","x":40.91,"y":13.96,"w":39.16,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"phones","x":83.16,"y":13.96,"w":36.07,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"can","x":122.31,"y":13.96,"w":17.76,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"use","x":143.05,"y":13.96,"w":17.75,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"two","x":163.77,"y":13.96,"w":17.04,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"types","x":183.9,"y":13.96,"w":26.25,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"of","x":213.23,"y":13.96,"w":9.05,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"satellite:","x":225.45,"y":13.96,"w":40.29,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"●","x":83.4,"y":39.4,"w":6.66,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"geostationary","x":104.67,"y":39.4,"w":66.15,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"satellites","x":173.81,"y":39.4,"w":42.71,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"at","x":219.6,"y":39.4,"w":9.05,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":"a","x":231.82,"y":39.4,"w":6.13,"s":11.04,"f":"sans"},{"t":